The eleven bundled source/header/license files are unchanged upstream material.
LIE selects the upstream Boost Software License 1.0 alternative; the original
Apache 2.0 alternative, dual notices and both full license texts are retained.
These files are not first-party MIT code and are not a system dependency.

src/binary64.c includes the pinned C shortest formatter and short parser with
private symbol prefixes. First-party MIT code independently supplies default
fixed/scientific spelling policy, closest integer spelling, JSON number syntax,
bounded full-span parsing and exact long-decimal nearest-even conversion.
The fast parser sees at most 17 significant digits; longer inputs use the exact
fallback, retaining 800 significant digits plus a sticky tail. Binary64 rounding
midpoints have at most 768 significant decimal digits. Input digits beyond the
retained prefix still influence exact midpoint decisions; they are not dropped.

MPFR/GMP are independent, installed QA oracles for tests/sampling only. They are
not linked into the ordinary server, bench, core or default CTest products.
No upstream model code, weights, sibling workspace source or DS4 artifact is
imported. This source increment requires host qualification separately from original-
weight GPU continuation, allocation-exact resource cost and matched performance.
